# Agent-harness config. The SHARED, deliberately-written parts are committed —
# settings.json, hooks, subagents, skills, rules — because they encode this
# repo's invariants (do not hand-edit generated files; run the gate before
# claiming done) and every contributor benefits from them.
#
# Everything else stays out. `settings.local.json` in particular carries
# personal choices such as permission mode, and committing a permission-bypass
# setting would silently disable another contributor's prompts on clone.
.claude/*
!.claude/README.md
!.claude/settings.json
!.claude/agents/
!.claude/skills/
!.claude/hooks/
!.claude/rules/
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/*.lock

# Subagent-driven-development scratch: ledger, task briefs, review packages.
# Session-local coordination state, never part of the product.
.superpowers/
# Written by `vercel link`. `.vercel/` holds the project and org ids; `.env.local`
# holds a short-lived OIDC token the CLI downloads. Neither is ours to commit,
# and the token in particular must not be.
.vercel
.env*.local
